        "text": "A best-effort, hand-authored attempt to find Broken Object Level Authorization with CodeQL's standard building blocks: global taint tracking from a RemoteFlowSource (the library's own notion of a routed request parameter / request data) into the key of an object lookup, where an ownership comparison acts as a BarrierGuard. This is NOT part of any CodeQL suite: it is the \"CodeQL can express guard dominance via BarrierGuard\" experiment for the codefix baselines (bench/baselines.py). It was written once, before looking at its results, and is not tuned per app."
